This repository carries two licences, because it carries two kinds of work.

## Kernel patches — GPL-2.0-only

`patches/` modifies the Linux kernel. Those changes are a derivative work of the
kernel and are therefore licensed **GPL-2.0-only**, the same terms as the code
they patch. The full text is in `LICENSE.GPL-2.0`.

This is not a choice made here: the kernel's licence requires it. If you
distribute a binary kernel built from these patches, you must also offer the
corresponding source.

    SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only

## Everything else — MIT

`tools/`, `components/` and `docs/` are original work and are licensed **MIT**;
the full text is in `LICENSE.MIT`. Individual components may carry their own
LICENSE file, which governs that component.

    SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT

## Third-party material

See `NOTICE.md` for what this repository deliberately does not contain, and
`docs/upstream-sources.md` for every external project this port draws on, with
its licence.
